      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:1:4:85:6",
      "text": [
        " مَنْ أَشْرَكَ مَعَ إِمَامٍ إِمَامَتُهُ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ مَنْ لَيْسَتْ إِمَامَتُهُ مِنَ اللَّهِ كَانَ مُشْرِكاً بِاللَّهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Muhammad Bin Al Husayn, from Muhammad Bin Sinan, from Talha Bin Zayd, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The one who associates with an Imam<sup>asws</sup> in his<sup>asws</sup> Imamate from the Presence of Allah<sup>azwj</sup>, the one whose Imamate isn’t from Allah<sup>azwj</sup>, would be an associater (Mushrik) with Allah<sup>azwj</sup>’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          " 6. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Muhammad ibn al-Hassan from Muhammad ibn Sinan from Talha ibn Yazid from abu ‘Abdallah (a.s.) who has said the following. “Whoever would share the leadership of a Lead with Divine Authority without Divine authority is a polytheist.”"
        ]
      }
    },
